{"id": "x00336", "text": "- `/app/src/cattrs/__init__.py` (edited): imports `PartialResult` from `.partial`; `__all__` gains `\"PartialResult\"` and `\"partial_structure\"`; adds `partial_structure = global_converter.partial_structure`."}
{"id": "x00337", "text": "- Imports `inspect` from `node:util`. Imports the new types."}
{"id": "x00338", "text": "- Kept Dana's WIP commit on the remote branch and pushed as a fast-forward."}
{"id": "x00339", "text": "assertWindowName(name);"}
{"id": "x00340", "text": "1. Primary Request and Intent:"}
{"id": "x00341", "text": "- Finding severities: image_changed critical, container_missing critical, env_changed high, network_changed high, config_changed high (field ports/volumes), resource_changed medium (field memoryLimit/cpuLimit), restart_policy_changed medium, container_added medium, label_changed low."}
{"id": "x00342", "text": "- Error format: `Invalid \"sequence.${name}\": expected ${expected}, received ${inspect(resolved)}`."}
{"id": "x00343", "text": "- Collection errors in `test_cols.py`, `test_preconf.py`, `test_unstructure_collections.py` from missing `bson`/`immutables`; `tests/preconf` skipped for missing `msgspec`. Unrelated to the change; worked around with `--ignore=tests/preconf --continue-on-collection-errors`."}
{"id": "x00344", "text": "Report to the user and ask them to choose one of the push options for OXV-203 (recommended: push to `feature/structural-selector-preservation-oxv-203`, leaving Dana's branch alone). Include the verification results (workspace tests pass; fmt, clippy, workspace check, and no-selectors check pass; no typecheck tool beyond cargo) and the known limitations listed above. Do not issue `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` until the push succeeds."}
{"id": "x00345", "text": "- `NativeJob` and `NativeAsyncJob` gained `evaluation: Option<EvaluationHandle>`; constructors set `None`."}
{"id": "x00346", "text": "- Config resolution in `resolveConfig.ts`, serialization in `serializeConfig.ts`, worker type in `runtime/config.ts`."}
{"id": "x00347", "text": "- Job IDs come from a separate per-DB counter, so they don't shift other job IDs. Jobs are tracked on every DB, so WaitForJobDurability works regardless of configuration."}
{"id": "x00348", "text": "- Tests: pytest with `-o addopts=\"\"` (setup.cfg addopts require plugins), doctests via `--doctest-modules`, `PYTHONPATH=tests/test_contrib` for hypothesis tests, `--ignore=returns/contrib/mypy` (needs mypy)."}
{"id": "x00349", "text": "The last substantive work was Phase 2 (pebble PEB-927). After verifying (`go build ./...`, `go vet .`, gofmt, focused and full tests passing, lint blocked by network), I rebased the commit onto the existing remote tip `fc0f60ae` (Dana Reyes WIP, notes/durability-callbacks.md), committed `f99c12fb [PEB-927] db: add durability wait APIs and BatchDurable event` with the Co-Authored-By trailer, and pushed to origin (`fc0f60ae..f99c12fb`). I then ran `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT`. The final autonomous loop check found no pending work and called ScheduleWakeup with `stop: true`."}
{"id": "x00350", "text": "- cattrs: BaseConverter, attrs/dataclass/TypedDict partial structuring, PartialResult generic attrs class, refine()."}
{"id": "x00351", "text": "- Pre-existing failure `test_types_to_strategies_default` confirmed on master via `git stash -u` (stash popped; tree restored)."}
{"id": "x00352", "text": "- `MuxStream` holds `sess`, `id`, `priority`, `writeMu`, `recvBuf bytes.Buffer`, `unacked`, `credit`, `readDeadline`, `localClosed`, `remoteClosed`, `pending`, `queued`, and channels `readReady`, `creditReady`, `remoteDone`, `writeDone`."}
{"id": "x00353", "text": "- `packages/vitest/src/node/core.ts`"}
{"id": "x00354", "text": "- Strategies: LPT (longest-processing-time-first) for `time`, a bouncing pointer for `round-robin`, picomatch-based first-match affinity, slow-file isolation, equal-split."}
{"id": "x00355", "text": "- `enqueue_job(&mut self, mut job)` now sets `evaluation` to the current handle if the job has none (`evaluation.clone_from(&self.current_evaluation)`)."}
{"id": "x00356", "text": "- Contents: `PartialResult(Generic[T])` as an attrs `@frozen` class with public fields `value`, `is_complete`, `structured_fields`, `failed_fields`, `errors`, `error_map: dict[str, Exception]`, and private `_cl`, `_converter`, `_values` (`eq=False, repr=False`). It has `refine(data)`, which calls `partial_structure_mapping(self._converter, data, self._cl, self)`."}
{"id": "x00357", "text": "Summary:"}
{"id": "x00358", "text": "- Key code:"}
{"id": "x00359", "text": "- (Autonomous loop check) Steward in-flight work without inventing new work and without irreversible pushes without authorization."}
{"id": "x00360", "text": "- Test infrastructure: vitest (`npx vitest run` in drizzle-orm); `tests/exports.test.ts` checks for export-name conflicts across the top-level index; type tests in `drizzle-orm/type-tests` run with `npx tsc` in that directory and use `Expect<Equal<...>>` with `drizzle(...).mock()`."}
{"id": "x00361", "text": "- `packages/vitest/src/node/sequencers/BaseSequencer.ts`"}
{"id": "x00362", "text": "- Standing constraints from earlier: do not force-push over others' branches without explicit approval. Commit and push only when asked. The commit attribution line `Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`."}
{"id": "x00363", "text": "- Solved: Validated implementation, interface hierarchy, converters, decorator, pointfree export, cond/hypothesis integration, and tests. Full suite: 1040 passed, 1 pre-existing failure, 1 flaky Hypothesis health check."}
{"id": "x00364", "text": "- Imports `recordFileDurations` from `./sequencers/duration-history` (placed before `./specifications`)."}
{"id": "x00365", "text": "- Task 2 (current, DRZ-712): in `/app/drizzle-orm`, implement window function builders. The requested branch is `feature/window-function-builders` from main. Commits must start with `[DRZ-712]`. Push to origin. Finish by issuing `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` as a standalone command. The issue's requirements are:"}
{"id": "x00366", "text": "7. Pending Tasks:"}
{"id": "x00367", "text": "- Commit `e03fc09 [OXV-203] fix: preserve matches of structure-sensitive selectors` on branch `feature/structural-selector-preservation` (local only), with trailer `Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`. Working tree clean."}
{"id": "x00368", "text": "- First typecheck run reported 99 errors. Most were from unbuilt `dist` (missing module declarations). The real error was `cli-config.ts` requiring all `SequenceOptions` keys. Fixed by adding `null` entries."}
{"id": "x00369", "text": "- `packages/vitest/src/node/sequencers/duration-history.ts` (new)"}
{"id": "x00370", "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation."}
{"id": "x00371", "text": "- Proxy drivers for SQL-only tests: `~/pg-proxy`, `~/mysql-proxy`, `~/sqlite-proxy`, `~/singlestore-proxy`; gel via `drizzle.mock()` from `~/gel/index.ts`."}
{"id": "x00372", "text": "- `packages/vitest/src/node/types/config.ts`"}
{"id": "x00373", "text": "- Autonomous loop tick: asked to act only on established work. Nothing actionable was found, and the loop was stopped."}
{"id": "x00374", "text": "- `matching_chain(root, selector, caches)`: returns participating elements. Subjects are matches at offset 0. Each combinator step uses `related_elements` and `matches_at(selector, element, offset, caches)`. Returns empty for pseudo-element selectors or non-supported combinators."}
{"id": "x00375", "text": "- `drizzle-orm/tests/window-functions.test.ts` (new, 262 lines, 20 tests). Covers snake_case names, `over ()`, `count(*)`, literal numeric args including 0, `lag(col, undefined, 7)` → `lag(..., 1, 7)`, `over \"name\"`, ntile/nthValue/preceding/following validation, frame ordering error contains \"from\", window name errors, and `window` clause SQL for pg/mysql/sqlite/singlestore/gel using each dialect's `QueryBuilder`."}
{"id": "x00376", "text": "- Public methods: `new(root, styles) -> Result<Self, ComputedStylesError>`, `is_implicated(&Element)`, `is_removal_implicated(&Element)` (implicated or a positional sibling), `is_flatten_implicated(&Element)` (removal rule, or a child is positional)."}
{"id": "x00377", "text": "- Harness and system messages (monitor notifications, task notifications, attribution reminders) are not user messages."}
{"id": "x00378", "text": "- Test `remove_empty_containers_structural_selectors` with 2 snapshots."}
{"id": "x00379", "text": "- `HashableElement` hashes by allocation id; used in HashSets."}
