{"id": "x00392", "text": "If you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /opt/emx/cc/projects/-app/c4823bdf-2dfa-4ac6-8f4c-9636ce26a78a.jsonl"}
{"id": "x00393", "text": "- Current task (RET-292, returns repo at /app): implement a `Validated` error-accumulating container with `Valid` and `Invalid` subtypes. `Invalid` stores errors as a tuple; `apply` accumulates errors left-to-right; `bind` short-circuits. Requirements include `from_failure` wrapping a 1-tuple, `swap` (`Valid(x)→Invalid((x,))`, `Invalid(errs)→Valid(errs)`), `from_validated` returning the same instance, per-element `alt` on `Invalid`, `__match_args__` on both subtypes, container-interface integration (equality, repr, do-notation, unwrap, failure, value_or, from_value), `bind_validated` method plus pointfree export, `from_result`, `combine`, `combine_n`, `result_to_validated` / `validated_to_result` converters, and a `validated` decorator with an `exceptions` parameter that preserves the wrapped name. Implementation hints: `ValidatedLikeN` must not extend DiverseFailableN (swap breaks double_swap_law); update `returns/methods/cond.py`, `returns/contrib/hypothesis/containers.py`, `returns/pointfree/__init__.py`."}
{"id": "x00394", "text": "It sits after `get_structure_hook`, with `..  versionadded:: NEXT`."}
{"id": "x00395", "text": "- Current task, ARC-151 (arcane repo at /app): implement drift detection comparing live container state against environment baselines. Create branch `feature/drift-detection-baselines` from main, commit with `[ARC-151]` prefix, push to origin, then finish with the standalone command `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT`. Status: implementation committed and pushed under a different branch name (see Current Work). The echo has been run."}
